# the root task's shell, typed at over the serial console: the prompt, the
# commands, line editing, a test run from inside the shell, and halting with
# success.
< jos shell; type help for the commands
< jos>
> help
< bench [rounds]
< jos>
> echo hello from the console
< hello from the console
# two backspaces take "xd" back out before the rest is typed.
> echo fixd\b\bxed
< fixed
# ctrl-u throws the whole line away.
> rubbish\uecho cleared
< cleared
# ctrl-c abandons a line without running it.
> echo never\c
< ^C
# an arrow key's escape sequence adds nothing to the line.
> \e[Aecho arrows
< arrows
> mem
< capability slots free
> list
< calls_reach_the_longest_waiting_receiver
> test timed
< ok 2 a_timed_receive_takes_what_arrives_in_time
< all passed
> bench 200
< 200 call/reply round trips
# processes: the boot modules, and hello started from the shell, exiting,
# refused the machine, and faulting on an address it has nothing mapped at.
> modules
< hello (
> run hello
< hello from a process of its own
< hello exited with 0
> run hello 1
< hello exited with 1
> run hello 550561120256
< hello faulted: PageFault
> run nosuch
< run: no such boot module
> nosuchcommand
< unknown command nosuchcommand; try help
> halt 0
< jos: machine halted by userspace (code 0x0)
